- ## digression
+ ## digression

- - `digression.StackTrace.legend: Map[Text, Text]` is now keyed by the bare glyph (`λ`, `ⲛ`, `δ`,
-   `⁅⁆`) rather than the glyph padded to two characters (`λₙ`, `ⲛ `, `δ `); it is derived from the
-   new `digression.StackTrace.Marker.all`. `ⲛ` is described as "constructor" (previously "class
-   initializer"); `Σ` is listed as before, `ζ` is no longer produced, and `Ξ`, `Λ`, `ι`, `ℓ`,
-   `⇢`, `≔`, `∂`, `⊡` and `⊙` are listed. (#2442)
- - `digression.StackTrace.rewrite(name: String, method: Boolean = false): Text` changes its output
-   for these inputs: `$adapted` marks the preceding `λ` as `Λ` (`lam$$anonfun$1$adapted` →
-   `lam.Λ₁()`, previously `lam.λ₁.adapted()`); `<clinit>` and `$init$` → `ι` (previously
-   unchanged and `.init.`); `$lzyINIT`, `$lzy` and `$lzyHandle` → `ℓ` (previously `#ℓ`, `#lzy`,
-   `#lzyHandle`); `protected$`, `inline$` and `$accessor` → `⇢`; `$_setter_$` → `≔`;
-   `$retainedBody` → `⊡`; `$outer` → `⊙`; `$$Lambda` → `#λ`/`.λ`; `$uXXXX` → the character;
-   `$mc…$sp` consumes the tags, so `apply$mcII$sp` → `applyΣ(Int -> Int)()` (previously
-   `applyΣ(Int -> Int)IIζ()`) and the parameters of a specialized method of arity above one are
-   now in order with the result last (`apply$mcJII$sp` → `applyΣ((Int, Int) -> Long)()`, likewise
-   `scala.runtime.java8.JFunction2$mcJII$sp` → `((Int, Int) => Long)`); a bare `$sp` is no longer
-   `ζ`; `Play$$cue` (an expanded private name) → `Play.cue()` with one separator (previously
-   `Play..cue()`), though `$$` followed by an operator encoding still decodes as the operator;
-   `initial$` and `$_avoid_name_clash_$`, which the compiler no longer emits, are no longer
-   rewritten to `ι` and `′`. Numbers after `$`, operators, `$anonfun`, `$anon`, `<init>`,
-   `super$`, `$extension`, `$direct`, `$default`, `$package` and module classes are unchanged.
+ - `digression.StackTrace.legend: Map[Text, Text]` tiene ahora como clave el glifo desnudo (`λ`,
+   `ⲛ`, `δ`, `⁅⁆`) en lugar del glifo rellenado hasta dos caracteres (`λₙ`, `ⲛ `, `δ `); se deriva
+   del nuevo `digression.StackTrace.Marker.all`. `ⲛ` se describe como «constructor» (antes «class
+   initializer»); `Σ` aparece como antes, `ζ` ya no se produce, y aparecen `Ξ`, `Λ`, `ι`, `ℓ`,
+   `⇢`, `≔`, `∂`, `⊡` y `⊙`. (#2442)
+ - `digression.StackTrace.rewrite(name: String, method: Boolean = false): Text` cambia su salida
+   para estas entradas: `$adapted` marca la `λ` precedente como `Λ` (`lam$$anonfun$1$adapted` →
+   `lam.Λ₁()`, antes `lam.λ₁.adapted()`); `<clinit>` y `$init$` → `ι` (antes sin cambios y
+   `.init.`); `$lzyINIT`, `$lzy` y `$lzyHandle` → `ℓ` (antes `#ℓ`, `#lzy`, `#lzyHandle`);
+   `protected$`, `inline$` y `$accessor` → `⇢`; `$_setter_$` → `≔`; `$retainedBody` → `⊡`;
+   `$outer` → `⊙`; `$$Lambda` → `#λ`/`.λ`; `$uXXXX` → el carácter; `$mc…$sp` consume las
+   etiquetas, así que `apply$mcII$sp` → `applyΣ(Int -> Int)()` (antes `applyΣ(Int -> Int)IIζ()`)
+   y los parámetros de un método especializado de aridad mayor que uno van ahora en orden con el
+   resultado al final (`apply$mcJII$sp` → `applyΣ((Int, Int) -> Long)()`, e igualmente
+   `scala.runtime.java8.JFunction2$mcJII$sp` → `((Int, Int) => Long)`); un `$sp` desnudo ya no es
+   `ζ`; `Play$$cue` (un nombre privado expandido) → `Play.cue()` con un solo separador (antes
+   `Play..cue()`), aunque `$$` seguido de la codificación de un operador sigue decodificándose como
+   el operador; `initial$` y `$_avoid_name_clash_$`, que el compilador ya no emite, ya no se
+   reescriben como `ι` y `′`. Los números tras `$`, los operadores, `$anonfun`, `$anon`, `<init>`,
+   `super$`, `$extension`, `$direct`, `$default`, `$package` y las clases de módulo no cambian.

=   `super$`, `$extension`, `$direct`, `$default`, `$package` and module classes are unchanged.
